            r"To extract coefficients from a product $Z$ write $Z=\sum_{j<J}q_jB_0^j+\varepsilon B_0^J$ with $J=2r$, and put $\widehat h_j\equiv q_j+\rho_j$ centered in $[-B_0/2,B_0/2)$ with carry $\rho_{j+1}=(q_j+\rho_j-\widehat h_j)/B_0\in\{0,1\}$; the residual identity $\sum_{k\ge j}h_kB_0^{k-j}=\sum_{k\ge j}q_kB_0^{k-j}+\rho_j+\varepsilon B_0^{J-j}$ shows $\widehat h_j=h_j$ and ends with $\rho_J+\varepsilon=0$.",
